course: dictionary
lesson: 10589
title: Underneath: place, layers and hidden feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word underneath tells you where something is: directly below or under something, often covered or hidden by it. «In Bradford, Tariq's dad is strict and religious and warm underneath.» Underneath here does not mean under a bed. It means his kindness is hidden behind his strict outside.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «The baby teeth sit in the mouth, and underneath them, packed into the jaw, the grown-up teeth are already waiting.» The words underneath them tell you exactly where the grown-up teeth are: below the baby teeth, hidden from view.
explain: Underneath can also mean the lower side or bottom surface of something. «The Amazon giant water lily has leaves held up by stiff ribs underneath.» Check your meaning by swapping in under. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Underneath means directly below or under something, often covered or hidden by it.
fact: Underneath can mean the bottom side of something, as in «stiff ribs underneath» a leaf.
fact: Underneath can also mean hidden behind how someone seems on the outside, as in «warm underneath».
fact: In science, layers are described with underneath: soil underneath grass, rock underneath soil, water underneath ice.
fact: Safety rule: never hide underneath a car, and never stand underneath a falling load.
exercise: «In Bradford, Tariq's dad is strict and religious and warm underneath.» What does underneath suggest here? | *He is kind, though his kindness is hidden behind his strict manner | He is a dentist | He lives under a bridge | He is loud and angry all the time
exercise: In science, rock lies underneath soil. What is the layer that sits below soil? | *Rock | Clouds | Grass | Leaves
exercise: The safety rule says never stand underneath a falling load. Why is this important? | It is a good place to rest | Loads prefer to be watched | It makes the load heavier | *It is dangerous, because the load could fall on you
test: «The baby teeth sit in the mouth, and underneath them the grown-up teeth are waiting.» Where are the grown-up teeth? | Inside the coach | Outside the mouth | On top of the baby teeth | *Below the baby teeth, hidden in the jaw
test: Which word could replace underneath in «a coach has luggage space underneath» without changing the meaning? | *Under | Over | Beside | Above
exam: Read «Headlines are written to grab you, so read the story underneath; a shocking post on no trusted news site is probably fake.» What does underneath mean here? | Upside down | *The full story below the headline, which the headline may hide | A trusted news site | Shouting loudly
